  "details": "Going into 3rd Person, invoking \"Immobilize\" from VRC Animator Locomotion Control, then pressing tab to free-rotate the camera, then pressing tab *again* causes a multitude of unusual behaviours.\n\n- The first time tab is pressed, the camera unlocks and you can rotate around your avatar normally.\n\n- The second time tab is pressed, the avatar's head snaps to the direction you were looking in (correctly) but its *body* *does not*, instead remains pointing the same way it did before\n\n- Pressing tab a third time causes the avatar's head to snap to the direction your camera was facing, *plus the difference between the current rotation and the last time you hit tab*. The body still remains unmoved.\n\n- Continuously pressing tab causes these rotations to add up and your avatars head to snap to seemingly random directions, until Immobilize is disabled.\n\n- Other actions that cause the head to start following the camera's direction, such as exiting third person (by scrolling all the way up, pressing F5, etc) have a similar effect to pressing tab here.\n\nIn addition to Immobilize locking one axis of the camera, this now also makes your avatar look like it has its head screwed on backwards.",
